<!-- [EN Sync v7.0] -->
<div class="lf-trap-card" data-trap="T1" data-hq-id="LF-T1-AI">
            <div class="lf-trap-header">
                <span class="lf-trap-badge">T1</span>
                <span class="lf-trap-diff">⭐⭐</span>
                <span class="lf-trap-id">LF-T1-AI</span>
            </div>
            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">Xiao Ming is facing southeast. He turns 90 degrees to the right, then 45 degrees to the left. What direction is he facing now?</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common Mistake</span>
                    <span >Common mistake: East. Students mistakenly think that after turning right 90 degrees he faces southwest, and then turning left 45 degrees brings him back to east, ignoring the order of direction changes and angle calculation.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="lf-trap-right">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct Approach</span>
                    <span >Correct answer: South. Steps: First facing southeast, after turning right 90 degrees he faces southwest; then turning left 45 degrees, from southwest turning left 45 degrees points to south.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="lf-trap-note">💡 Turning right is clockwise, turning left is counterclockwise. Draw a direction diagram step by step!</div>
            </div>
        </div>
<div class="lf-trap-card" data-trap="T2" data-hq-id="LF-T2-AI">
            <div class="lf-trap-header">
                <span class="lf-trap-badge">T2</span>
                <span class="lf-trap-diff">⭐⭐⭐</span>
                <span class="lf-trap-id">LF-T2-AI</span>
            </div>
            <div>
                <div class="lf-trap-q">The school is north of the park, and the library is west of the school. If starting from the library and wanting to go to the park, which direction should you go?</div>
                <div class="lf-trap-wrong">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Common Mistake</span>
                    <span >Common mistake: Go north. Students directly see that the park is north of the school and assume they should go north from the library, ignoring that the library is west of the school, so they need to go east to the school first, then north.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="lf-trap-right">
                    <span class="lf-ex-label">Correct Approach</span>
                    <span >Correct answer: Go east first, then go north. Explanation: The library is west of the school, so from the library go east to the school, then from the school go north to the park.</span>
                </div>
                <div class="lf-trap-note">💡 Different starting points mean the route must be connected; don't skip the intermediate point!</div>
            </div>
        </div>
